WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.730
Funafuti atoll, Tuvalu: a thin ring of
coral islets around a lagoon in the Pacific.

2
00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:11.170
The nation's mean elevation is
just 2 metres above sea level.

3
00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:13.530
There are no hills to retreat to.

4
00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:18.830
Here, the sea is nearly 15 centimetres
higher than 30 years earlier.

5
00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:23.570
And it is rising 1.5 times
faster than the global average.

6
00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:26.730
So what can people on islands this low do?

7
00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:28.310
Build walls round every island?

8
00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:31.030
Is it already too late?

9
00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:35.350
In this mission, you'll explain why
sea level is rising around the world.

10
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:39.510
Then you'll judge how Tuvalu's government
and communities are responding to the

11
00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:40.570
threat.

12
00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:45.400
Your mission: decide what an island
community can do as the sea rises.
